  <h2 id="security">9. Security</h2>
  <p>We protect personal data with measures such as these:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Encrypted connections (HTTPS) to the app, careers pages, and our website, and encryption of stored data at rest.</li>
    <li>
      In the app, only team members of a company can access its data, and admin-only actions are checked on our servers.
      Resumes are kept in private storage, and every request to open one is checked to make sure it comes from a
      signed-in team member of the right company.
    </li>
    <li>
      You don't create a password for Emploist. Sign-in codes and invitation links are stored only in hashed form, and
      sign-in codes expire after 5 minutes and allow 3 tries.
    </li>
    <li>Strict security headers and content security policies. Careers pages run in a sandbox that blocks scripts.</li>
    <li>
      Checks on untrusted content. Customers' careers page code runs in worker threads with time and memory limits.
      Uploaded files are checked by their contents and size, and resumes are read in worker threads with limits. Rich
      text, email designs, and SVG logos are cleaned of unsafe code.
    </li>
    <li>Rate limits on sign-in, the app, careers pages, and applications, and a spam trap on application forms.</li>
    <li>Cookies, sign-in secrets, and invitation links are removed from our request logs.</li>
    <li>Card details are handled by Dodo.</li>
    <li>Regular backups, with the ability to restore them, and an incident response process.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    No system is perfectly secure, and we can't guarantee that personal data will never be accessed without permission.
    If a breach affects your personal data, we'll notify you and the relevant authorities as the law requires. For
    Customer Data, we'll notify affected customers without undue delay, and within 72 hours of becoming aware of the
    breach, as our <a href="/terms/#data-processing">data processing terms</a> describe.
  </p>

  <h2 id="your-rights">10. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Access</strong> your personal data and get a copy of it</li>
    <li><strong>Correct</strong> data that's inaccurate or incomplete</li>
    <li><strong>Delete</strong> your data</li>
    <li><strong>Restrict</strong> how we use it</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Take it with you</strong> (portability): receive it in a machine-readable format, or have it sent to
      another provider
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Object</strong> to how we use it, including when we rely on legitimate interests.
      See <a href="#right-to-object">Your right to object</a>.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> where we rely on it, without affecting what we did before</li>
    <li><strong>Complain</strong> to a data protection authority</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    These rights have limits. For example, we may need to keep some data to meet legal obligations. If we can't fully
    meet a request, we'll explain why.
  </p>

  <h3>How to make a request</h3>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a>, ideally from the email address on your
    Emploist account. We may need to confirm your identity before we act. We'll respond within the time the law sets,
    which is generally one month. We won't charge you, unless the law allows a fee, for example for requests that are
    clearly unfounded or excessive.
  </p>

