  <h3>India</h3>
  <p>
    Under India's Information Technology Act and its rules on sensitive personal data, you can review the information
    you've given us and ask us to correct or update it. You can also choose not to give us information, or withdraw
    consent you've given, by emailing us. If you do, we may not be able to provide Emploist to you. These rights cover
    the information we collect from you as controller. For an application you sent to an employer, contact the employer.
  </p>
  <p>
    These rules treat passwords as sensitive personal data, and define a password broadly, as a secret code or key used
    to gain access. So the sign-in secrets listed in <a href="#sensitive-information">Sensitive information</a> may count
    as sensitive personal data. We collect them only to sign people in, keep sign-in codes and invitation link secrets
    only in hashed form, and share them only as <a href="#subprocessors">Sharing and subprocessors</a> describes.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can raise any grievance with our Grievance Officer, Navaneeth CT,
    at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a>. We'll acknowledge it within 24 hours and resolve it
    within 15 days of receiving it.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you're in India, then as India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 comes into force, you'll also have
    the rights it gives, such as to get a summary of your personal data and how we use it, to have it corrected or
    erased, to have your grievances addressed, to nominate someone to act for you, and, after first raising a grievance
    with us, to complain to the Data Protection Board of India.
  </p>

