      <tr>
        <td><code>emploist.session_token</code></td>
        <td>Keeps you signed in</td>
        <td>7 days, renewed while you use the app</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>emploist.state</code></td>
        <td>Protects your sign-in with Google or Microsoft</td>
        <td>5 minutes, and removed once you're signed in</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    On app.emploist.com, which uses HTTPS, both names start with <code>__Secure-</code>. Both cookies are HttpOnly, so
    scripts on the page can't read them, and they're sent only to the app, not to careers pages.
  </p>
  <p>
    The app also uses your browser's local storage to remember your theme (<code>emploist-theme</code>) and whether the
    sidebar is collapsed (<code>emploist-sidebar-collapsed</code>). These stay in your browser and aren't sent to us.
  </p>
  <p>
    Emploist sets no cookies on careers pages, and scripts don't run on them. If an employer's own careers page design
    loads content from other websites, those websites may set their own cookies,
    as <a href="#applicants">For job applicants</a> explains. emploist.com sets no cookies, uses no local storage, and runs
    no analytics.
  </p>
  <p>
    Because these cookies and storage are needed for the app to work, or only remember choices you make, they don't need
    your consent, and we don't show a cookie banner. If you block cookies, you won't be able to sign in.
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">12. Children</h2>
  <p>
    Emploist is for businesses. You must be 18 or older to use the app. We don't knowingly collect personal data from
    children as a controller. If you believe a child has given us personal data, email us and we'll delete it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Employers decide who can apply for their jobs. If an employer accepts applications from people under 18, the
    employer is responsible for meeting the law's requirements, such as getting a parent's consent where needed.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">13. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy when Emploist or the law changes, and we'll change the "Last updated" date at the top of
    this page. If a change is material, we'll email everyone with an Emploist account at least 30 days before it takes
    effect. If the law requires a change sooner, we'll give as much notice as we can.
  </p>

